{"results":[{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q8NI08","uniProtkbId":"NCOA7_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Nuclear receptor coactivator 7"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"140 kDa estrogen receptor-associated protein"}},{"fullName":{"value":"Estrogen nuclear receptor coactivator 1"}}]},"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q6DFV7"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"11971969"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17391516"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"25330068"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"38593795"}],"value":"Transcriptional coactivator which enhances the transcriptional activities of several nuclear receptors including ESR1, THRB, PPARG and RARA (PubMed:11971969). Inhibits the activity of the vacuolar-type ATPase (V-ATPase) by inducing disassembly of the V-ATPase complex (PubMed:38593795). Protects the Golgi apparatus lumen from excess acidification by inhibiting V-ATPase ATP hydrolytic activity through interaction with V-ATPase catalytic subunit ATP6V1A, maintaining optimal conditions for glycosylation enzymes (By similarity). Required to stabilize V-ATPase V1 subunits ATP6V1B2 and ATP6V1A at membrane sites (By similarity). Involved in protection against oxidative damage (PubMed:17391516, PubMed:25330068). Involved in urine acidification (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q6DFV7"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"25330068"}],"value":"Exhibits oxidation resistance activity (PubMed:25330068). Protects neuronal cells from oxidative stress with weaker neuroprotective activity than isoform 5 (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Isoform 1"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q6DFV7"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"25330068"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"30478388"}],"value":"Exhibits oxidation resistance activity (PubMed:25330068). Protects neuronal cells from oxidative stress with stronger neuroprotective activity than isoform 1 (By similarity). Inhibits endosome-mediated viral entry by inhibiting fusion of the viral and endosomal membranes and subsequent nuclear translocation of viral ribonucleoproteins (PubMed:30478388). Promotes increased cytoplasmic vesicular acidification, lysosomal protease activity and the degradation of endocytosed material (PubMed:30478388)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Isoform 5"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q6DFV7"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17391516"}],"value":"Predominantly nuclear following estradiol stimulation (PubMed:17391516). Localizes to the nucleus and cytoplasm in the absence of estradiol (PubMed:17391516). Recruited to the cis-Golgi network and trans-Golgi network membranes in a Rab-dependent manner (By similarity)"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17391516"}],"value":"Nucleus","id":"SL-0191"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"17391516"}],"value":"Cytoplasm","id":"SL-0086"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q6DFV7"}],"value":"Golgi apparatus, cis-Golgi network membrane","id":"SL-0068"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Peripheral membrane protein","id":"SL-9903"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q6DFV7"}],"value":"Golgi apparatus, trans-Golgi network membrane","id":"SL-0267"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Peripheral membrane protein","id":"SL-9903"}}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","molecule":"Isoform 5","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"30478388"}],"value":"Cytoplasm","id":"SL-0086"}}]}],"features":[{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":114,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":157,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"LysM","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"PROSITE-ProRule","id":"PRU01118"}]},{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":781,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":942,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"TLDc","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"PROSITE-ProRule","id":"PRU01234"}]},{"type":"Region","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":46,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Disordered","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"SAM","id":"MobiDB-lite"}]},{"type":"Region","location":{"start":{"value":161,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":188,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Disordered","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"SAM","id":"MobiDB-lite"}]},{"type":"Region","location":{"start":{"value":324,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":416,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Disordered","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"SAM","id":"MobiDB-lite"}]},{"type":"Coiled coil","location":{"start":{"value":4,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":29,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}]},{"type":"Compositional bias","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":12,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Basic and acidic residues","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"SAM","id":"MobiDB-lite"}]},{"type":"Compositional bias","location":{"start":{"value":25,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":38,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Polar residues","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"SAM","id":"MobiDB-lite"}]},{"type":"Compos